# Operating «<שם בעברית>» (the `<id>` app)

<Vendor client>, the vendor's own Linux client, inside the office (ai/context/wrapped-official-app.md):
- its screen is the console's tile;
- its headless side is behind `http://<id>:<adapter port>` (`<interface>.v1`);
- its sign-in lives in the volume `<id>_home`.

## What you can do from here

```bash
./bbox <short name> status [--json]     # up, and signed in
./bbox <short name> flow                # what it did, as it happens
curl -s http://<id>:<adapter port>/v1/health
```

## Rules

- Act through the contract (`<interface>.v1`), never through the vendor's protocol or its files.
- An outward action (a message to a person, a post) runs only on the owner's word.
- The sign-in is the owner's: never sign out, and never change the account.

## Traps

- The client's sign-in survives a restart only in the volume. A new volume is a new sign-in.
